<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU Court upholds 75 mln ECU fine against Tetra Pak.</title>
<headline>EU Court upholds 75 mln ECU fine against Tetra Pak.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Court of Justice rejected on Thursday an appeal by Swedish carton marker Tetra Pak against a 75 million European currency units fine imposed on the company by the European Commission in 1991, a Court official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Court dismisses the appeal&quot;, the official told Reuters. Tetra Pak was told to pay costs.</p>
<p>The Commission decided to fine Tetra Pak in July 1991 after it concluded the company had broken European Union competition rules by &quot;bullying&quot; rivals and slashing prices to control the European market for over a decade.</p>
<p>An earlier attempt by Tetra Pak to have the fine annuled had already been dismissed by the European Court of First Instance, the EU's lower court.</p>
</text>
